{
  "chapter": "capstone/building-it",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "Build bottom-up: tools and data, context, runtime, durability, interface. That is the",
    "order things must exist in, not the order they demo in.",
    "Nine tools, not nineteen. Every tool is a permission and every description is prompt text",
    "billed each turn.",
    "issue_credit takes an order id and re-derives the amount; send_reply has no recipient",
    "argument. Removing a parameter beats validating one, and poisoning and injection arrive",
    "at the same fix from different directions.",
    "Every class four or five tool ships with a paired read, or 'unknown' is permanently",
    "unresolvable.",
    "Route before retrieving: semantic, aggregation, relationship, live state \u2014 four systems,",
    "four strategies.",
    "Split the corpus by trust. The poisoned article can still rank first and still cannot",
    "reach a write tool.",
    "Workflow code decides; activity code discovers. Model calls and tool calls are always",
    "activities.",
    "Put the tenant in the workflow id: structural tenancy and queue routing in one decision."
  ],
  "policy": {
    "maxTools": 9,
    "forbiddenArgs": [
      "amountCents",
      "recipient",
      "tenantId"
    ],
    "routes": {
      "semantic": "vector",
      "aggregation": "sql",
      "relationship": "graph",
      "live-state": "api"
    },
    "buildOrder": [
      "tools",
      "context",
      "runtime",
      "durability",
      "interface"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
